/**
 * CONSTRAINT IDENTIFICATION
 *   constraint_id: ai_governance_legitimacy__technocratic_optimization_reading
 *   human_readable: Technocratic Optimization Reading of AI Governance Legitimacy
 *   domain: political_theology/technology_governance
 *
 * SUMMARY:
 *   The standing arrangement under contest is the governance settlement in
 *   which AI development earns its legitimacy by demonstrating aggregate
 *   welfare gains, efficiency improvements, and innovation output — with
 *   ethical considerations entering as weighted parameters to be balanced
 *   against feasibility, and authority vested in whoever demonstrates
 *   performance. This file instantiates the technocratic_optimization_reading
 *   of the ai_governance_legitimacy kernel as a clean, epsilon-invariant
 *   constraint: the arrangement it describes coordinates a real, globally
 *   distributed development enterprise around shared performance metrics,
 *   while the costs of that coordination land disproportionately on
 *   populations with no seat in the drafting rooms. The manifest hypothesized
 *   rope; the refined structural read is tangled_rope, because the same
 *   structure that coordinates (benchmark regimes, capital allocation, expert
 *   gatekeeping) also carries identified uncompensated payers and is held in
 *   place by active enforcement (competitive discipline against ethical
 *   restraint, regulatory capture, consensus gatekeeping). That divergence
 *   from the manifest hypothesis is recorded in uke_scope and left
 *   unreconciled — the claim and the metrics are independently authored
 *   facts. KEY AGENTS (by structural relationship): - ai_development_firms:
 *   agenda-setting beneficiary (institutional/arbitrage) — sets the
 *   optimization agenda and collects the surplus - venture_capital_investors:
 *   beneficiary (powerful/arbitrage) — funds and disciplines the pace -
 *   high_skill_technical_workforce: beneficiary (moderate/mobile) — premium
 *   wages inside the frame - early_adopter_enterprises: beneficiary
 *   (powerful/constrained) — productivity gains, lobbying weight -
 *   displaced_workers: primary payer (powerless/trapped) — bears transition
 *   costs counted as aggregate gains - digitally_unconnected_communities:
 *   payer (powerless/trapped) — excluded from AI-mediated services, hosts the
 *   physical footprint - algorithmically_profiled_individuals: payer
 *   (powerless/trapped) — scored and gated by opaque systems -
 *   technical_evaluation_bodies: agenda-setter with beneficiary position
 *   (institutional/identity_locked) — administers the metric regime their
 *   standing depends on - captured_regulatory_agencies: nominal overseer with
 *   beneficiary position (institutional/arbitrage) -
 *   dignity_first_civil_society: excluded voice (organized/constrained) -
 *   technology_policy_analysts: analytical observer (analytical/analytical)
 *
 */

