% COORDINATION_FUNCTION: Shared efficiency and capability metrics coordinate a globally distributed AI development enterprise: benchmarks give competing labs a common measure of progress, capital markets a basis for allocation, and governments a shorthand for distinguishing serious systems from vaporware. Evaluation infrastructure is built once and reused everywhere instead of per-lab.
% TRANSFER_FUNCTION: Moves decision authority over AI deployment from affected publics and workers to technical experts and firm leadership; moves the costs of optimization — job displacement, infrastructural exclusion, profiling exposure — onto populations without seats at the drafting table; moves the resulting surplus to capital holders and high-skill technical labor.
% ABSENT_VOICES: Displaced workers, digitally unconnected communities, algorithmically profiled individuals, and dignity-first ethical traditions — including the magisterial voice of the encyclical — are absent from the rooms where legitimacy criteria are set. They appear in optimization documents only as 'constraints', 'externalities', or 'transition issues'. Democratic-pluralist proponents of inclusive public reason are likewise outside the expert consultation loop.
% DISAPPEARANCE_RATIONALE: If the efficiency-legitimacy criterion vanished overnight, capital allocation, research agendas, hiring patterns, procurement rules, and regulatory posture would all reorganize around whichever legitimacy principle replaced it. The current scale and pace of the AI buildout is premised on performance metrics conferring permission; withdraw that premise and deployment slows, funding reprices, and the contest between the sibling readings moves from the margins to the center.
% FOUNDING_PROBLEM: Early AI governance faced a genuine coordination problem: no shared standard existed for evaluating systems, safety practices were fragmented across labs, and competitive pressure pushed toward deployment without any common basis for allocating trust, capital, or regulatory attention. Performance-and-welfare criteria offered a common currency for progress and a workable basis for all three allocations.
% FOUNDING_PROBLEM_CORROBORATION: Standards bodies and development firms attest the evaluation-coordination problem remains live, citing benchmark fragmentation and safety-evaluation gaps. From outside the benefiting parties, independent AI-safety researchers, labor economists studying displacement exposure, and the multilateral AI-governance process attest that the problem's persistence does not license the further move of locating legitimacy itself in aggregate performance — the magisterial and democratic-pluralist readings both dispute precisely that step, and published distributional analyses corroborate that realized gains and losses have diverged from the aggregate account.
narrative_ontology:disappearance_verdict(ai_governance_legitimacy__technocratic_optimization_reading, world_rearranges).
