/* ==========================================================================
   5. GENERATIVE COMMENTARY
   ========================================================================== */

/**
 * LOGIC RATIONALE:
 *   Extractiveness is authored at 0.36 — moderate, and deliberately assessed by this reading's own lights over the fixed referent of the standing technocratic settlement: the reading itself acknowledges real aggregate gains and treats some costs as legitimate transition overhead, but its own framework cannot make the concentrated, uncompensated, and recurring losses of displaced workers, unconnected communities, and profiled individuals disappear from the ledger. Suppression is 0.58: this is soft, structural coercion rather than overt force — competitive punishment of first-mover ethical restraint, expert-consensus gatekeeping that reframes dignity-first proposals as feasibility failures, and capture that converts oversight into template compliance. Alternatives are not erased; they are starved, which is why accessibility_collapse sits at 0.45 rather than mountain-range values — the dignity-first and deliberative framings remain fully articulable and visibly defended, but practically foreclosed in institutional terms. Theater_ratio at 0.45 reflects the well-documented growth of principles documents, ethics boards, and responsible-AI teams whose output volume has decoupled from deployment decisions; the metric-regime core of the constraint remains functional, so the ratio stays below the piton threshold while trending upward. Resistance at 0.52 reflects sustained labor organizing, algorithmic-justice litigation, and binding-regulation campaigns (EU-style statutes) that the arrangement must actively absorb. The measurement series run on one shared time grid (points 0, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15 of a 15-year interval beginning at deep-learning commercialization); point 15 carries projected basis, all earlier points observed. All three tracked series rise together: extraction accumulates as deployment outruns compensation, theater grows as principles substitute for restraint, and the enforcement machinery matures as capture and gatekeeping professionalize — the suppression_requirement series is authored because the story specifically tracks the build-out of that enforcement capacity, not merely shifting extraction.
 *
 * PERSPECTIVAL GAP:
 *   The seats compute differently by construction. From the agenda-setting beneficiary seat (development firms, evaluation bodies), the arrangement presents as the coordination achievement that made the field legible and fundable — a rope-shaped world in which metrics solved a genuine collective-action problem. From the payer seats (displaced workers, unconnected communities, profiled individuals), the identical structure presents as a closed loop in which the currency of legitimacy is controlled by the parties who profit from it and their losses are pre-classified as friction. The dual-positioned institutional seats (evaluation bodies, captured agencies) sit between: they administer a frame they did not choose and collect standing from maintaining it. The engine computes these per-seat classifications from the structural data; nothing in the authored claim adjudicates between them.
 *
 * DIRECTIONALITY LOGIC:
 *   Beneficiary declarations drive the derivation: development firms, investors, the high-skill workforce, and adopter enterprises sit near the beneficiary end (low d), with the firms nearest zero as the direct collectors. Victim declarations drive the opposite pole: displaced workers, unconnected communities, and profiled individuals sit near the full-target end, and their trapped exit options push them further toward full-target than mobile payers would sit — a worker who could retrain cheaply bears less effective extraction than one anchored by mortgage and age. The two dual-role institutional seats complicate the picture in ways the derivation handles through their secondary beneficiary position: evaluation bodies and captured agencies are nominally neutral administrators whose effective directionality tilts toward the frame they administer, and the identity lock on the evaluation bodies means their exit option cannot arbitrage the frame away without dissolving themselves. Spatial scope amplifies: the arrangement operates globally while verification of its welfare claims is jurisdictionally fragmented, which scales effective extraction upward at the payer seats. No directionality overrides are authored — the beneficiary/victim structure plus exit options already yields the correct relationships, and the schema's override mechanism keys on power atoms too coarsely to differentiate the two institutional administrator seats without mislabeling the firms that share their atom.
 *
 * MANDATROPHY ANALYSIS:
 *   The founding problem — fragmented evaluation, no common currency for trust and capital allocation — is genuinely still live, which blocks any mandatrophy resolution: the coordination function is real and currently load-bearing, so this is not a vestigial constraint maintained by inertia. The classification prevents mislabeling in both directions: reading the arrangement as pure rope (the manifest hypothesis, and the reading's own self-presentation) would erase the identified payers whose costs ride the same structure; reading it as pure snare would erase the real coordination achievement that makes the extraction possible and partially legitimate even to its critics. The tangled-rope claim holds both facts. The forward-looking risk the temporal series documents is proxy substitution: as theater_ratio climbs past 0.4, the metric regime risks becoming self-referential — optimizing benchmarks rather than welfare — at which point the founding problem's solution would have detached from its purpose and the constraint would begin drifting toward the degraded end of the lifecycle. The R5 mismatch consumer should watch status=contested x verdict=world_rearranges: the parties dispute whether the founding problem still licenses this arrangement, while the world demonstrably remains organized around it.
 */

